{"retrieved_on": "2026-11-13", "source_url": "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=%28EXT_ID%3A32908284+OR+EXT_ID%3A32909055+OR+EXT_ID%3A32909959+OR+EXT_ID%3A32911665+OR+EXT_ID%3A32912474+OR+EXT_ID%3A32917666+OR+EXT_ID%3A32939979+OR+EXT_ID%3A32960880+OR+EXT_ID%3A32961010+OR+EXT_ID%3A32961340+OR+EXT_ID%3A32968067+OR+EXT_ID%3A32971255+OR+EXT_ID%3A32975552+OR+EXT_ID%3A32975661+OR+EXT_ID%3A32978307+OR+EXT_ID%3A32984550+OR+EXT_ID%3A32994452+OR+EXT_ID%3A32994889+OR+EXT_ID%3A32999867+OR+EXT_ID%3A33009413+OR+EXT_ID%3A33012378+OR+EXT_ID%3A33015372+OR+EXT_ID%3A33031522+OR+EXT_ID%3A33036490+OR+EXT_ID%3A33037212+OR+EXT_ID%3A33042271+OR+EXT_ID%3A33043150+OR+EXT_ID%3A33049577+OR+EXT_ID%3A33065387+OR+EXT_ID%3A33067442+OR+EXT_ID%3A33083571+OR+EXT_ID%3A33094213+OR+EXT_ID%3A33103967+OR+EXT_ID%3A33116300+OR+EXT_ID%3A33125022+OR+EXT_ID%3A33129141+OR+EXT_ID%3A33136540+OR+EXT_ID%3A33139755+OR+EXT_ID%3A33142892+OR+EXT_ID%3A33147166+OR+EXT_ID%3A33151319+OR+EXT_ID%3A33169099+OR+EXT_ID%3A33180899+OR+EXT_ID%3A33188996+OR+EXT_ID%3A33204028+OR+EXT_ID%3A33204939+OR+EXT_ID%3A33205106+OR+EXT_ID%3A33208341+OR+EXT_ID%3A33209648+OR+EXT_ID%3A33217963+OR+EXT_ID%3A33227719+OR+EXT_ID%3A33241040+OR+EXT_ID%3A33243898+OR+EXT_ID%3A33243986+OR+EXT_ID%3A33244514+OR+EXT_ID%3A33257700+OR+EXT_ID%3A33261057+OR+EXT_ID%3A33267819+OR+EXT_ID%3A33283212+OR+EXT_ID%3A34112736%29+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core&pageSize=100", "hitCount": 1, "resultList": {"result": [{"id": "33204028", "source": "MED", "pmid": "33204028", "pmcid": "PMC7884739", "fullTextIdList": {"fullTextId": ["PMC7884739"]}, "doi": "10.1038/s41416-020-01122-x", "title": "Deep learning in cancer pathology: a new generation of clinical biomarkers.", "authorString": "Echle A, Rindtorff NT, Brinker TJ, Luedde T, Pearson AT, Kather JN.", "authorList": {"author": [{"fullName": "Echle A", "lastName": "Echle", "firstName": "Amelie", "initials": "A", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0789-9509"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Medicine III, University Hospital RWTH Aachen, Aachen, Germany."}]}}, {"fullName": "Rindtorff NT", "lastName": "Rindtorff", "firstName": "Niklas Timon", "initials": "NT", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ), Heidelberg, Germany."}]}}, {"fullName": "Brinker TJ", "lastName": "Brinker", "firstName": "Titus Josef", "initials": "TJ", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-3620-5919"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "National Center for Tumor Diseases (NCT), German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ), Heidelberg, Germany."}]}}, {"fullName": "Luedde T", "lastName": "Luedde", "firstName": "Tom", "initials": "T", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6288-8821"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Infectious Diseases, University Hospital Duesseldorf, Düsseldorf, Germany."}]}}, {"fullName": "Pearson AT", "lastName": "Pearson", "firstName": "Alexander Thomas", "initials": "AT", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Section of Hematology/Oncology, Department of Medicine, The University of Chicago, Chicago, IL, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Kather JN", "lastName": "Kather", "firstName": "Jakob Nikolas", "initials": "JN", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-3730-5348"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Medicine III, University Hospital RWTH Aachen, Aachen, Germany. jkather@ukaachen.de."}, {"affiliation": "German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ), Heidelberg, Germany. jkather@ukaachen.de."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-3620-5919"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-3730-5348"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-6288-8821"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0789-9509"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "4", "volume": "124", "journalIssueId": 3113815, "dateOfPublication": "2021 Feb", "monthOfPublication": 2, "yearOfPublication": 2021, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Br J Cancer", "title": "British journal of cancer", "essn": "1532-1827", "issn": "0007-0920", "isoabbreviation": "Br J Cancer", "nlmid": "0370635"}, "printPublicationDate": "2021-02-01"}, "pubYear": "2021", "pageInfo": "686-696", "abstractText": "Clinical workflows in oncology rely on predictive and prognostic molecular biomarkers. However, the growing number of these complex biomarkers tends to increase the cost and time for decision-making in routine daily oncology practice; furthermore, biomarkers often require tumour tissue on top of routine diagnostic material. Nevertheless, routinely available tumour tissue contains an abundance of clinically relevant information that is currently not fully exploited. Advances in deep learning (DL), an artificial intelligence (AI) technology, have enabled the extraction of previously hidden information directly from routine histology images of cancer, providing potentially clinically useful information. Here, we outline emerging concepts of how DL can extract biomarkers directly from histology images and summarise studies of basic and advanced image analysis for cancer histology. Basic image analysis tasks include detection, grading and subtyping of tumour tissue in histology images; they are aimed at automating pathology workflows and consequently do not immediately translate into clinical decisions. Exceeding such basic approaches, DL has also been used for advanced image analysis tasks, which have the potential of directly affecting clinical decision-making processes. These advanced approaches include inference of molecular features, prediction of survival and end-to-end prediction of therapy response. Predictions made by such DL systems could simplify and enrich clinical decision-making, but require rigorous external validation in clinical settings.", "affiliation": "Department of Medicine III, University Hospital RWTH Aachen, Aachen, Germany.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "review-article", "Review", "Journal Article"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (German Research Foundation)", "grantId": "SFB CRC1382/P01, SFB-TRR57/P06, LU 1360/3-1", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Deutsche Krebshilfe (German Cancer Aid)", "grantId": "70113864", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "European Research Council", "grantId": "771083", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "RWTH Aachen University (Rheinisch-Westfälische Technische Hochschule Aachen)", "grantId": "691906", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Neoplasms", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "PA", "qualifierName": "pathology"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "TH", "qualifierName": "therapy"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Prognosis"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Decision Making"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Image Processing, Computer-Assisted", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Biomarkers, Tumor", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "AN", "qualifierName": "analysis"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Deep Learning"}]}, "chemicalList": {"chemical": [{"name": "Biomarkers, Tumor", "registryNumber": "0"}]}, "subsetList": {"subset": [{"code": "IM", "name": "Index Medicus"}]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Open access", "availability